---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Work with me - hellointernet.lol">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <section class="cg-panel page-hero">
      <div class="cg-kicker">engagement filter</div>
      <h1>Bring me the constraint.</h1>
      <p>
        I work best when something real is stuck: a workflow that keeps eating time, a product surface that needs to ship,
        or a decision bottleneck that needs structure instead of another meeting.
      </p>
      <div class="cg-meta">
        <span class="cg-status active">build + diagnose</span>
        <span class="cg-status in-progress">short path to signal</span>
        <span>less discovery theater, more visible movement</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-grid tight">
      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">good fit</div>
        <h2>Decision-makers with a real problem</h2>
        <p>You know something is dragging, but the exact fix is still fuzzy. That is usually enough to start.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">best work</div>
        <h2>Custom systems over generic packages</h2>
        <p>I help when the problem does not fit cleanly inside a standard agency process or off-the-shelf workflow.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">handoff goal</div>
        <h2>Remove the bottleneck, then get out of the way</h2>
        <p>The point is not dependency. The point is a cleaner operating state than the one you started with.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="page-grid">
      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">what usually shows up</div>
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>a messy internal process with too many manual steps</li>
          <li>a missing tool between people, systems, or decisions</li>
          <li>an AI/product idea that needs implementation reality instead of hype language</li>
          <li>a small team blocked by invisible technical debt or operational drag</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">not a fit</div>
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>long discovery arcs with no artifact pressure</li>
          <li>tool shopping without a defined constraint</li>
          <li>work that is mostly alignment theater</li>
          <li>teams that want certainty before they are willing to learn anything</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="cg-panel section-stack">
      <div>
        <div class="cg-kicker">starting packet</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">The first email should include three things.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="page-grid tight">
        <article class="cg-card page-card">
          <div class="cg-kicker">1</div>
          <h3>What is not working</h3>
          <p>Name the friction plainly. Slow is fine. Messy is fine. Vague pain is still useful.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="cg-card page-card">
          <div class="cg-kicker">2</div>
          <h3>What better would look like</h3>
          <p>Not a perfect spec. Just the future state you wish existed.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="cg-card page-card">
          <div class="cg-kicker">3</div>
          <h3>When it matters</h3>
          <p>Urgency changes shape. Deadlines, hiring windows, launches, or internal pressure all count.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="cg-list">
        <a class="cg-command" href="mailto:joshua@fullyautomated.enterprises">
          <span>$ contact</span>
          <span>joshua@fullyautomated.enterprises</span>
        </a>
        <a class="cg-command" href="/work">
          <span>$ inspect</span>
          <span>hellointernet.lol/work/</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
